# Packages repo-lag should not report, one name per line.
#
# Not all lag is a bug. Omarchy deliberately pins and repackages some things,
# and those show as "behind" forever because the version strings genuinely
# differ. Listing them here keeps the report short enough to stay worth reading.
#
# A pkgrel-only gap is the usual sign of a deliberate pin: same upstream
# version, different trailing -N. For example, at the time of writing:
#
#   1password   installed 8.12.36-2   vs   AUR 8.12.36-42
#
# That is Omarchy repackaging 8.12.36, not a stale build -- a reasonable
# candidate for this list. Left commented out so it stays your call.
#
# 1password

# Shadowed omarchy builds, each verified 2026-09-18 as harmless on THIS machine.
# [omarchy] is last in pacman.conf, so these never install; that is correct here.
#
#   ghostty*  omarchy 1.3.1-3 is a strict SUBSET of extra 1.3.1-2 -- same upstream
#             1.3.1, 658 files vs 668, missing the man pages and HTML/md docs.
#
#   linux-firmware-cirrus
#             omarchy 20260810-3 is a strict SUPERSET of core -2: +99 Cirrus smart
#             amp blobs (cs35l41/54/56) keyed to ASUS/HP/Lenovo/Dell subsystem IDs.
#             This is a System76 Oryx Pro (Clevo 1558:66a2) with a Realtek ALC1220
#             and no cs35l* modules -- zero of the 99 files match any ID on this
#             box. Revisit if the machine ever changes.
ghostty
ghostty-shell-integration
ghostty-terminfo
linux-firmware-cirrus
